# Windows 8 Single-User Hardening Guide (Complete with Commands)

This document defines a strict, single-user hardening posture for Windows 8. The system is assumed to be end-of-life, insecure by default, and must be deliberately reduced, constrained, and verified.

## Chapter 1 — Threat Model
One user. One machine. No background trust. Primary threats include silent network egress, unauthorized persistence, and metadata leakage.

## Chapter 2 — Pre-Hardening Enumeration

Enumerate users, services, network state, scheduled tasks, and data layout.

```cmd
net user
sc query state= all
netstat -ano
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v
```

## Chapter 3 — User and Privilege Control

Ensure a single local administrator account. Disable remote access and enforce elevation prompts.

```cmd
net user
reg add "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server" /v fDenyTSConnections /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System /v ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin /t REG_DWORD /d 2 /f
reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System /v EnableLUA /t REG_DWORD /d 1 /f
```

## Chapter 4 — Service Reduction

Disable telemetry, diagnostics, discovery, sharing, and unused services.

```cmd
sc stop WerSvc
sc config WerSvc start= disabled
sc config SSDPSRV start= disabled
sc stop SSDPSRV
sc config Spooler start= disabled
```

## Chapter 5 — Network Constrainment

Enable firewall and enforce default-deny.

```cmd
netsh advfirewall set allprofiles state on
netsh advfirewall set allprofiles firewallpolicy blockinbound,blockoutbound
netsh advfirewall firewall add rule name="Allow DNS" dir=out action=allow protocol=UDP remoteport=53
```

## Chapter 6 — Scheduled Task Elimination

Disable background tasks used for persistence.

```cmd
schtasks /query /fo LIST /v
schtasks /change /disable /tn "\Microsoft\Windows\Application Experience\ProgramDataUpdater"
```

## Chapter 7 — Data and Metadata Control

Disable indexing, prefetching, and behavioral caching.

```cmd
sc stop WSearch
sc config WSearch start= disabled
sc stop SysMain
sc config SysMain start= disabled
```

## Chapter 8 — Verification

Re-enumerate and validate idle behavior.

```cmd
sc query state= all
netstat -ano
schtasks /query
```

## Chapter 9 — Operational Posture

Operate deliberately. Re-verify after every change.
